Japan CX Director 　* New Position

Customer Experience (CX) Strategic Leadership, Everpure &nbsp;

Role Summary &nbsp;

The Japan Service Director is a senior CX leader accountable for long-term value creation with Everpure's most strategic Japanese enterprise customers. The core mission is to be a trusted advisor to these customers, producing mutual innovation and measurable outcomes. This leader owns the Japan CX strategy, including the 3-year plan and customer success motion, and represents Everpure at the executive level in Japan, including major escalations.&nbsp;

The role is a matrix lead across customer-dedicated team members and works with global CX, Sales, Engineering and partner organizations. It covers the full CX framework: Technical Support (TS), Professional Services (PS), Advanced Services, PEAK, Customer Advocacy, Portfolio, and Customer Success.

&nbsp;

What You Will Be Doing &nbsp;

Drive strategic customer outcomes in Japan &nbsp;

• Deliver a world-class service experience that exceeds Japanese customer expectations, including expectations around quality, responsiveness and proactive communication.&nbsp;

• Own the Japan CX strategy and 3-year plan, including the customer success motion and plan, in partnership with global CX and portfolio leaders.&nbsp;

• Partner with Sales to execute 1-3-year integrated account plans. Join account planning meetings for top customers and other strategic accounts as required, and act as the single point of accountability for the Japan customer experience across the full services portfolio.&nbsp;

• Maintain a deep, face-to-face presence with named customers, building trust-based relationships with key stakeholders and executives.&nbsp;

• Partner with the cross-functional delivery team (SAM, DSE, TAM, CSM and Channel Partners) as a peer of the other team leaders, aligning efforts across functions to deliver consistent, high-quality service to Japanese customers.

• Partner with the designated executive sponsor(s) to achieve their objectives and outcomes for Japan accounts.&nbsp;

• Develop and implement customer retention strategies for the Japan market.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Escalations and customer advocacy &nbsp;

• Represent Everpure at major Japanese escalations, working with the service support team and functional owners through critical care programs, with proactive communication and executive involvement for swift resolution.&nbsp;

• Champion Japanese customer requirements into Engineering, Quality, product roadmaps and service offer development.&nbsp;

• Advocate for and influence Japan-specific processes and workflows (Lifecycle Services or Business Critical Services) so that global processes meet local expectations.&nbsp;

• Advocate for EG1(Evergreen1) customers and services, applying strong financial acumen.&nbsp;

• Sponsor Continuous Improvement and Problem Management trends for Japan accounts, driving swift root cause analysis and remediation.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Customer journey, growth and innovation &nbsp;

• Design and plan the service customer journey (Lifecycle Management) for Japan accounts.&nbsp;

• Understand each customer's core business goals with Sales, and identify opportunities for value co-creation, growth, and expansion.

• Drive account-based innovation to improve customer perception of solution and service value, ease of doing business, and continuous improvement.&nbsp;

